  "name": "t23-g4-join-budget",
  "description": "T23 / G4 row 11 join budget, worst-case-sized evidence. It runs the same eight-client g4-workload scene/population/cuts as t23-g4-workload: 256 active plus 4096 sleeping bodies (4352 total), two multi-region column cuts, a round-robin edit stream, and two blasts. Every client takes the real late-join baseline; client 7 alone is shaped to the exact G3 profile (1 MiB/s, 100 ms RTT, 20 ms jitter, 2% loss), while clients 0-6 use transparent proxies so the workload phase remains unshaped. A joining replica receives the dependency-complete baseline and then one current motion keyframe at the barrier; it must not receive the live 20 Hz motion feed before it confirms the baseline, because those supersedable datagrams can consume the shaped link and delay reliable baseline/control traffic. The harness measures client 7's actual compressed baseline bytes and connect-to-ready time and enforces <=16 MiB and <=30 s without reducing the workload. `restart_check` is intentionally omitted because t23-g4-workload already covers cold-restart recovery; this fixture isolates the shaped join measurement.",
